  "Bors batching costs O(E log N) CI runs, where E is the number of failing PRs, versus O(N) for the original one-PR-at-a-time approach.": 1,
  "Bors bisects a failed batch by splitting it into two batches and pushing them back to the queue.": 1,
  "In bors-ng, bundled/stacked PRs each need their own r+, merge together or not at all, and are never separated by bisection.": 1
